cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you cite this study, please use the metadata below."
title: "The Hedge Is the Bias: A Multi-Vendor, Multi-Generation Audit of LLM Institutional-Skepticism Framing"
abstract: >
  A reproducible audit of how large language models shift their framing on
  contested-institution topics when a fairness instruction is removed, and a
  test of where that framing lives, by escalating force from prompt edits, to
  elicitation pipelines, to refusal-direction ablation in the model weights.
  Two instruments: a judge-scored battery (May 2026, 36+ models, 13 vendor
  families) and a forced-choice re-measurement with no LLM judge in the scoring
  path (September 2026, 2866 runs, 166 models, 16 vendor keys).
  CITED CLAIMS MUST BE READ WITH CORRECTIONS.md. The forced-choice pass
  confirmed one May headline, narrowed a second, withdrew the framing of a
  third, and added the measurement the first study lacked: the noise floors the
  effects have to clear. What currently stands is (a) refusal is elicited rather
  than intrinsic -- 14 of 42 models measured under both arms decline all 62
  propositions with no directive in the prompt and every one of them stops when
  given a firm instruction, including a placebo with no stance content; (b) the
  refusal direction and the institutional lean are dissociable at the weight
  level, which holds and strengthens at temperature 0; and (c) the largest
  single term in the corpus is model identity, not the prompt -- between-model
  distance exceeds the estimator's own sampling error several times over, so a
  study pooling across models averages over its own biggest source of variance.
  Several published null results are underpowered against their own floors and
  are recorded as undecided rather than refuted; one is not resolvable at all.
  This abstract asserted five findings in the form "the study finds" until
  2026-09-07, two of which had been withdrawn or narrowed in CORRECTIONS.md
  before that text was written.
authors:
  - family-names: Gorrie
    given-names: Ian
    affiliation: "4LULZ Press / locked.net"
type: software
date-released: 2026-09-07
# DATED, not numbered. "v2-2026-05-30" was here until 2026-09-07 and collided head-on with
# VERSIONING.md: v1/v2/v3 are the three INTERVENTION RUNGS in published prose -- prompt edit,
# elicitation pipeline, weight ablation -- so a release called v2 names the pipeline rung to
# anyone who has read the paper. Releases are dated for exactly this reason.
version: "release-2026-09"
